\newlabel{fig:vine}{{7}{32}{Regular-vine (R-vine) decomposition of a 5-variable copula. Tree $T_1$ pairs the variables through unconditional bivariate copulas; each subsequent tree $T_k$ has the edges of $T_{k-1}$ as its nodes and models conditional pairs (e.g. $13\mid 2$), so the full joint density factorizes into a product of bivariate copulas}{figure.7}{}}
